switch (mode) {
case 1: start();
case 2: stop();
        break;
}

This loop is meant to print every element of vector v, but it reads one element too far. Which line is the bug?
vector<int> v = {1, 2, 3};
for (size_t i = 0; i <= v.size(); ++i) {
    cout << v[i];
}

What order do the keys print in?
```cpp
#include <map>
#include <string>
#include <iostream>
int main() {
    std::map<int, std::string> m;
    m[3] = "three";
    m[1] = "one";
    m[2] = "two";
    for (auto& p : m) std::cout << p.first << ' ';
}
